Template: uplink-watchdog/primary
Type: string
Default: eth0
Description: Primary uplink interface
 The interface whose internet access is watched.

Template: uplink-watchdog/backup
Type: string
Default: wwan0
Description: Backup interface
 Any ifupdown interface. It is brought up only for webservice requests
 and while the VPN runs.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failover_after
Type: string
Default: 300
Description: Seconds without internet before failing over
 The primary must be unable to reach the internet continuously for this
 long.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failback_after
Type: string
Default: 0
Description: Seconds the primary must be healthy before failing back
 0 fails back on the first good check.

Template: uplink-watchdog/interval
Type: string
Default: 10
Description: Seconds between health checks
 Used while the primary is healthy.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failed_interval
Type: string
Default: 2
Description: Seconds between health checks while failed over
 A short interval makes the failback fast.

Template: uplink-watchdog/targets
Type: string
Default: 1.1.1.1 8.8.8.8 9.9.9.9
Description: Ping targets for the health checks
 Space-separated addresses. Any one answering counts as healthy.

Template: uplink-watchdog/notify_url
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Webservice URL for failover and failback events
 A JSON event is POSTed to this URL. Leave empty for no webservice. No
 DNS is used: put an IP address in the URL, or set the service address
 below.

Template: uplink-watchdog/poll_url
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Webservice URL to poll while failed over
 Fetched every poll interval with ?host=<hostname>; it answers vpn, none
 or stop. Leave empty to use the notification URL.

Template: uplink-watchdog/poll_interval
Type: string
Default: 300
Description: Seconds between polls of the webservice
 Used while failed over.

Template: uplink-watchdog/service_ip
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Address of the webservice's host name
 Used instead of DNS if the URLs contain a host name. Leave empty if they
 contain an IP address.

Template: uplink-watchdog/api_token
Type: password
Description: Webservice API token
 Sent as "Authorization: Bearer <token>". Leave empty for none. It is
 stored in /etc/default/uplink-watchdog, which only root can read.

Template: uplink-watchdog/vpn_start_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command to start the VPN
 Run (sh -c) on a "vpn" answer while the VPN isn't running. It must route
 the VPN over the backup itself.

Template: uplink-watchdog/vpn_check_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command to check the VPN
 A later "vpn" answer reruns the start command only if this exits non-
 zero.

Template: uplink-watchdog/vpn_stop_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command to stop the VPN
 Run on a "stop" answer and on failback.

Template: uplink-watchdog/primary_up_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command when the primary becomes healthy
 Run at once when the primary's health check changes from failing to
 passing, and for the first check after a start.

Template: uplink-watchdog/primary_down_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command when the primary stops being healthy
 Run at once when the primary's health check changes from passing to
 failing, without the failover delay.

Template: uplink-watchdog/backup_up_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command after the backup was brought up
 Run after each time the backup interface was brought up.

Template: uplink-watchdog/backup_down_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command after the backup was taken down
 Run after each time the backup interface was taken down, if it was up.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failover_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command on failing over
 Run before the backup is brought up for the failover notification.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failback_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command after failing back
 Run once the VPN is stopped, the notification was tried and the backup
 is down.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failback_stable_after
Type: string
Default: 300
Description: Seconds the primary must stay healthy after a failback
 After this long the stable command runs. A failed check restarts the
 wait.

Template: uplink-watchdog/failback_stable_cmd
Type: string
Default: 
Description: Command when the primary stayed healthy after a failback
 Run once after a failback, when the primary has passed its checks for
 the time above.
